From 21d07550cfca4f02b54ad9124d3f0bf353220f34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 02:02:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: create the ROCmFP4-FAST q8_1 MMVQ mat-vec pipelines
 and gate them to n <= 5 on AMD

lane-209 rank 7 (the FP4 verify residual, 803 vs 609 us per verify graph, lane-204 SS6). The selector
ggml_vk_get_dequantize_mul_mat_vec already LISTED GGML_TYPE_Q4_0_ROCMFP4_FAST in the q8_1 table and
ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq returned true for it on AMD, so quantize_y was computed on every FP4 mat-vec and
the selector then returned a pipeline that was never created (null) - ggml-vulkan.cpp fell back to the f32
dequant shader silently, paying the quantize cost for nothing. Same selector-without-pipeline shape
lane-204 flagged for mul_mm.

Port: mul_mat_vecq_funcs.glsl gains the ROCmFP4-FAST repack (same nibble layout as mxfp4, 17-byte block,
kvalues_rocmfp4 LUT) and its mmvq_dot_product (ue4m3 scale, exact-int LUT so d_a * d_b * int-dot is the
product the f32 path forms); mul_mat_vecq.comp gets K_PER_ITER 8 for the type; vulkan-shaders-gen.cpp emits
the q8_1 variants; ggml-vulkan.cpp creates the mat-vec and mat-vec-id pipelines.

Measured, test-backend-ops perf, q4_0_rocmfp4_fast 17408x5120, 3-round medians, engine-r5 (f32 path) vs
engine-r4c (MMVQ, this port) - lane-209 r4c/TBO-17408.txt: n=1 x0.998, n=2 x1.183, n=3 x1.335
(900.1 -> 674.3 us, 70.2 GB/s), n=4 x1.015, n=5 x1.316, n=8 x1.040 under the gate. The wider r4b ladder read
x0.796 at n=8 with MMVQ unbounded, which is why should_use_mmvq returns false for the type above n=5 on AMD;
n=1 stays MMVQ (a tie, and the upstream default for k >= 2048). The serve A/B on the julianmb
ROCmFP4-FAST file is the next step of the lane and is NOT claimed by this commit.

Taken-from: rocmfpx/main mul_mat_vecq_funcs.glsl + its :4867/:4931 registrations and shaders-gen :752/:624
Report: board/programs/local-inference/lanes/2026-09-02-lane-209-kernel-attacks-REPORT.md
